{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-23T16:28:47.917Z","data":{"text":"Implemented task 2 of the approval-digest change.\n\n**Core**\n- `approveSpec` now builds the digest after lint and before planning observation, calls the optional `review(digest)` port, throws `ApprovalDeclinedError` on `declined` before any write, returns `digest` on `ApproveResult`, and passes distinct flag ids + mode into the manifest.\n- `buildManifest` records `approvalFlags: { ids (deduped, sorted), mode }`; the field is omitted for planning-only callers (plan-queue) so the future report can distinguish approvals from queued plans.\n\n**CLI**\n- New `src/cli/confirm.ts` renders each flag and asks `Approve <id> with <n> flag(s)? [y/N]`, accepting only `y`/`yes`.\n- `approveCommand` takes injectable `confirm`, `isTerminal`, `ask`; prints the digest before sealing; under `--confirm` with flags refuses without a terminal (exit 1, nothing written) or prompts; the `Approved ...` line carries ` with <summary>`. Without flags `--confirm` never asks.\n- `showCommand` appends the digest/flag lines for an unapproved change and supports `--json` (details plus `digest`, null when approved).\n- `index.ts` registers `approve --confirm` and `show --json`.\n\n**Tests**: new `tests/approve-confirm.test.ts` and `tests/show-digest.test.ts` cover all acceptance lines, including the decline, refusal, and no-flag paths.\n\nTask verify passes (11 tests), and `pnpm verify` exits 0 (1464 + 88 tests, typechecks, build, lint). Result written to `.run/results/2.md`."}}
